Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Elizabeth Báthory\Nwas accused of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.95,0:00:04.10,Default,,0,0,0,,burning young maids\Nwith hot irons.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.10,0:00:06.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Of forcing others\Ninto freezing water.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.46,0:00:07.71,Default,,0,0,0,,People said young women
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.71,0:00:09.48,Default,,0,0,0,,were dying in\Nher household.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.67,0:00:11.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The rumours\Nreached the king.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.40,0:00:13.37,Default,,0,0,0,,He sent Hungary's\Nhighest official,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.37,0:00:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,György Thurzó,\Nto investigate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.90,0:00:17.27,Default,,0,0,0,,One December night,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.27,0:00:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,armed men arrived\Nat her manor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.70,0:00:21.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Báthory was\Neating supper.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.78,0:00:23.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Thurzó wrote that\Nhis men had found
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.69,0:00:26.15,Default,,0,0,0,,one girl dead and\Nanother dying.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.36,0:00:27.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Báthory was taken to the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.74,0:00:29.46,Default,,0,0,0,,fortress above her home.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.53,0:00:30.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Four servants,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.64,0:00:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,three women and\Na young man,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.52,0:00:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,were arrested as her\Nalleged accomplices.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.32,0:00:37.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Under torture,\Nthey confessed
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.02,0:00:38.71,Default,,0,0,0,,to dozens of killings.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.90,0:00:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Three were executed\Nwithin days.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.79,0:00:43.70,Default,,0,0,0,,But Báthory was\Nnever tried.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.89,0:00:45.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing was ever proven
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.14,0:00:46.52,Default,,0,0,0,,against her in court.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.73,0:00:49.27,Default,,0,0,0,,The case rested on\Nwitness testimony,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.34,0:00:51.21,Default,,0,0,0,,and much of it\Nwas hearsay.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.42,0:00:53.32,Default,,0,0,0,,The king pressed\Nfor a trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.53,0:00:55.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Thurzó prevented it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.43,0:00:56.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Thurzó had fought the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.65,0:00:58.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Ottomans beside\Nher husband.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.82,0:01:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Ferenc's dying\Nwish was that
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.60,0:01:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,his friend\Nwatch over her.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.56,0:01:05.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Many historians think\Nhe confined her quietly
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.60,0:01:07.18,Default,,0,0,0,,rather than risk\Nher beheading
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.18,0:01:08.93,Default,,0,0,0,,and the family's lands.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.14,0:01:10.98,Default,,0,0,0,,She died in confinement.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.19,0:01:13.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Then someone\Nadded the detail
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.02,0:01:14.76,Default,,0,0,0,,that would make\Nher infamous.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.20,0:01:16.54,Default,,0,0,0,,A century later,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.54,0:01:18.24,Default,,0,0,0,,a priest wrote\Nthat she bathed
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.24,0:01:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,in murdered girls' blood
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.51,0:01:20.86,Default,,0,0,0,,to keep her beauty.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.05,0:01:23.59,Default,,0,0,0,,No witness against her\Nhad described that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.80,0:01:25.63,Default,,0,0,0,,No court ever heard her.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.84,0:01:27.94,Default,,0,0,0,,But the legend\Nhad its monster:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.16,0:01:29.65,Default,,0,0,0,,the Blood Countess.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.20,0:01:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,History remembers\Nthe victors.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.97,0:01:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,We remember the rest.
